    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A cricket team is about to play two matches. The probability of the team having a win, a loss or a draw is 0.7, 0.1 and 0.2 respectively in each match. The possible results in the two matches are displayed in the probability tree diagram.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q20-tree",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 37 p37-q20-tree\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line width=0.8pt,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,inner sep=2pt}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (W) at (2.4,3);\n\\coordinate (L) at (2.4,0);\n\\coordinate (D) at (2.4,-3);\n\\draw (O)--(W) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.7$};\n\\draw (O)--(L) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.1$};\n\\draw (O)--(D) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.2$};\n\n\n\n\\foreach \\parent/\\height in {W/3,L/0,D/-3}{\n  \\draw (\\parent)--(5,\\height+1) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.7$};\n  \\draw (\\parent)--(5,\\height) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.1$};\n  \\draw (\\parent)--(5,\\height-1) node[midway,fill=white] {$0.2$};\n  \\node[anchor=west] at (5,\\height+1) {$W$};\n  \\node[anchor=west] at (5,\\height) {$L$};\n  \\node[anchor=west] at (5,\\height-1) {$D$};\n}\n\\node[fill=white] at (W) {$W$};\n\\node[fill=white] at (L) {$L$};\n\\node[fill=white] at (D) {$D$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 70,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 37,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 20, supplied tree on the left",
          "description": "An unshaded, left-to-right two-stage tree with three first-match branches and three second-match branches from each first-match result. All nine terminal labels are retained as W, L and D in source order.",
          "mathematics": "First-match probabilities are W:0.7, L:0.1 and D:0.2. Every first-match result has second-match branches W:0.7, L:0.1 and D:0.2. The twelve branch probabilities are supplied givens.",
